[CustomMessages]
BuildNow=Build the game now (one to two hours). The game may briefly open to capture missing map pictures.
RebuildShortcut=Rebuild Drakan
PlayShortcut=Drakan play folder
DiscTitle=Your game disc
DiscSubtitle=Where is your Drakan: The Ancients' Gates disc image?
DiscDescription=Choose your own PAL (SCES-500.06) or USA (SCUS-971.28, experimental) ISO. The game reads this file while running, so keep it in place. Most PC enhancements are unavailable with the USA disc and saves are separate.
DiscField=Disc image (.iso):
DiscFilter=Disc images (*.iso)|*.iso|All files (*.*)|*.*
DiscMissing=Choose your disc image (.iso) to continue.
DiscSmall=That file is too small. Choose the full game disc ISO.
PlayTitle=Play folder
PlaySubtitle=Where should the built game go?
PlayDescription=This folder holds the game, saves, settings, mods and HD textures. Rebuilds preserve your files. Uninstalling the builder leaves this folder in place. Intermediate files (about 2 GB) stay in the builder folder.
PlayField=Play folder:
PlayBadPath=Choose a separate play folder outside the builder's build folder. A drive root or the builder folder itself cannot be used.
OotfTitle=Drakan: Order of the Flame (optional)
OotfSubtitle=Add the first Drakan as a second campaign.
OotfDescription=Choose the installed PC game (the folder containing Dragon.rrc), a copy of the disc, or a disc image or ZIP. The builder converts its 13 campaign levels and 10 multiplayer arenas with their scenes and music. The title menu then offers both games. Leave the field empty to skip this step. Allow 3 to 8 minutes and about 1 GB before optional local transcription.
OotfBrowseFolder=Choose the Order of the Flame installation or copied disc folder
OotfBrowseImage=Choose the Order of the Flame disc image
OotfFolderButton=Choose install folder...
OotfImageButton=Choose disc image or ZIP...
OotfFilter=Disc images and ZIPs (*.mdx;*.iso;*.zip)|*.mdx;*.iso;*.zip|All files (*.*)|*.*
OotfBadFolder=The folder has no Dragon.rrc or SETUP\DATA1.CAB.
OotfBadFormat=Choose the installed game folder, a disc image (.mdx, .iso or .cue with .bin tracks), or a ZIP containing one.
OotfSmallFile=The file is too small. For a .cue/.bin disc image, choose the .cue file or track 1.
OotfMissing=That file or folder does not exist.
OotfInvalid=%1%n%nChoose your Order of the Flame source or leave the field empty to skip it.
OotfChecking=Checking your Order of the Flame files...
OotfRejected=Order of the Flame could not be added:%n%n%1%n%nThe main game will still build. To add the campaign later, rerun Setup or use -OotfSource <path>.
SubtitlesTitle=Order of the Flame subtitles
SubtitlesSubtitle=Choose the source of the scene captions.
SubtitlesDescription=Bundled captions match English recordings. For German, French, Italian or Spanish audio, use local transcription or supply ootf-subtitles.json for your copy. The first transcription downloads about 145 MiB and adds 5 to 15 minutes. Your recordings stay on this PC.
SubtitlesBundled=Use the included English subtitles or my transcript
SubtitlesGenerate=Generate subtitles from my recordings
DlssTitle=NVIDIA DLSS (optional)
DlssSubtitle=Upscaling and frame generation for NVIDIA RTX cards.
DlssDescription=Enable only if you have an NVIDIA RTX card. The build downloads the SDK from NVIDIA. Checking the box accepts the NVIDIA RTX SDKs License. See https://github.com/NVIDIA/DLSS/blob/v310.9.16/LICENSE.txt.
DlssOption=NVIDIA DLSS: I accept the NVIDIA RTX SDKs License
HdTitle=HD textures
HdSubtitle=Reuse a local pack or generate one from your disc.
HdDescription=Existing textures in local\textures or the play folder are reused. Generation uses Real-ESRGAN and downloads about 75 MB once. On a fast card it takes 17 to 32 min (about 2 GB), or 23 to 43 min with Order of the Flame (about 4 GB). Rebuild to resume.
HdOption=Generate HD textures after the build (requires Vulkan)
DefaultsTitle=Game options (optional)
DefaultsSubtitle=Choose the game's starting settings.
DefaultsDescription=Change these settings later with F1 in the game or in drakan.ini and drakan_input.ini in the play folder.
DefaultsMenus=Use modern PC menus. Clear to use the original PS2 menus.
DefaultsBow=Use the Order of the Flame bow controls: left click fires, right click aims.
DefaultsDual=Enable dual wielding (experimental).
DefaultsIssue=Show Report an Issue in the game menus.
OptionsTitle=Other options
OptionsSubtitle=Browser build, priority and VU1 compilation.
OptionsDescription=The browser build needs WSL with Ubuntu (wsl --install -d Ubuntu). The browser player uses the built folder and your ISO locally. The builder compiles VU1 microcode for the PS2’s second vector processor. The default uses about 2 GB of memory per compiler. Whole blocks can need 17 GB per compiler. The game runs at the same speed either way.
OptionsWeb=Also build the browser version (needs WSL with Ubuntu)
OptionsPriority=Compile at low priority to keep the PC responsive
OptionsLaunch=Start the game when the build finishes
OptionsVuWhole=Compile VU1 in whole blocks (older method, needs 24 GB or more)
CpuTitle=Build speed
CpuSubtitle=How much of this PC may the build use?
CpuDescription=This PC has %1 logical cores. Leave the field empty for automatic selection (half the cores, up to four). Each compiler needs up to 2 GB of memory. These settings affect the build. The affinity mask applies to Windows only.
CpuCores=CPU cores to use (empty = automatic):
CpuAffinity=Windows affinity mask (e.g. 0xFFF; empty = default):
CpuInvalidCores=Enter a number from 1 to %1, or leave the field empty.
CpuInvalidAffinity=Enter a nonzero hexadecimal mask of up to 16 digits, such as 0xFFF.
UpdateMismatch=This update does not match an existing Drakan PC Setup installation.
UpdateGameOpen=Close Drakan before retrying the update.
UpdateMissingDisc=The builder has no saved disc path. Use the Start menu shortcut to rebuild Drakan and choose your ISO, then retry.
UpdateBuildBusy=Setup could not lock the builder. Close any running build and retry the update.
UpdatePaths=For an update, the builder and play folders must match the installed copy.
UpdateBuilding=Rebuilding Drakan from your disc image...
UpdateFailed=The rebuild did not finish. Open Drakan to keep playing. If the shortcut no longer opens the game, rebuild Drakan from Start to recover it.%n%nBuild log: %1
UninstallSaves=Older saves may still be in the card folders (mc0, mc1, mc0_...) in:%n%1%n%nSetup could not copy them to the play folder. Uninstalling deletes that folder. Choose No to back up your saves first.%n%nUninstall anyway?
